<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;CHANNEL MOBILITY IMPROVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Channel Mobility Improvement is a concept that enhances the navigability and efficiency of waterways, allowing for smoother and more efficient transportation of vessels, and also refers to a game-changing concept in semiconductor manufacturing that improves the mobility of charge carriers within the channel."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;US 11430867&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PATENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"US 11430867 is a patent that revolutionized the semiconductor industry by introducing a game-changing concept of channel mobility improvement, enhancing the speed and performance of electronic devices."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEAM OF BRILLIANT MINDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Team of Brilliant Minds is a group of researchers and engineers who developed the concept of channel mobility improvement in semiconductor manufacturing, overcoming the limitations of traditional semiconductor design."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEMICONDUCTOR MANUFACTURING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Semiconductor Manufacturing refers to the realm where the quest for faster, more efficient, and more reliable devices drives innovation and research."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRONICS INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electronics Industry is the sector that benefits from the channel mobility improvement, enabling the creation of faster, more efficient, and more reliable devices."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States Army Corps of Engineers conducted a Navigation Channel Improvement Study in 1923, highlighting their role in channel improvement projects."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States Army Corps of Engineers is responsible for conducting studies on the optimization of waterway navigation and developing advanced dredging technologies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USS NIMITZ (CVN-68)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"USS Nimitz (CVN-68) is an aircraft carrier whose construction required significant channel mobility improvements to the waterway."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN MARY 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Queen Mary 2 is a cruise ship whose launch was facilitated by a comprehensive channel mobility improvement program."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNOVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Innovation is the driving force behind progress in both semiconductor manufacturing and maritime operations, pushing the boundaries of what is possible."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Progress is the outcome of continuous innovation in both semiconductor manufacturing and maritime operations, leading to advancements and improvements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCHERS AND ENGINEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Researchers and Engineers are the key players in both semiconductor manufacturing and maritime operations, driving innovation and solving complex problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIALS SCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Materials Science is a critical field in both semiconductor manufacturing and maritime operations, providing the foundational knowledge for innovations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVICE PHYSICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Device Physics is a fundamental area of study in semiconductor manufacturing, crucial for understanding and improving device performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATENT LAW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patent Law is a legal framework that protects innovations and ensures the intellectual property rights of inventors."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intellectual Property is the safeguard for innovations, ensuring that the creators of new technologies are recognized and protected."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENGINEERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Engineering is the application of scientific principles to solve practical problems, central to both semiconductor manufacturing and maritime operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DREDGING TECHNOLOGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dredging Technologies are advanced tools and methods used in maritime operations to improve waterway navigation and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDRAULIC DREDGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydraulic Dredgers are a type of advanced dredging technology used to remove sediment and debris from waterways."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUCTION DREDGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Suction Dredgers are another type of advanced dredging technology used to remove sediment and debris from waterways."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAVIGATION AIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Navigation Aids are tools and systems used to improve the safety and efficiency of maritime navigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDIMENT REMOVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sediment Removal is a critical process in channel mobility improvement, involving the removal of sediment and debris from waterways."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDERWATER OBSTACLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Underwater Obstacles are physical barriers in waterways that can impede navigation and require removal for improved mobility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwater Obstacles were removed as part of the Channel Mobility Improvement Program, improving navigational safety."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSIT TIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METRIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transit Times refer to the duration of travel through a waterway, a key metric in evaluating the efficiency of navigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARGO CAPACITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METRIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cargo Capacity is a measure of the amount of goods that can be transported through a waterway, a critical factor in maritime operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECISION AND CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precision and Control are essential for the successful transfer of a vessel to the water during ship launching."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATERWAY OPTIMIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waterway Optimization involves the systematic improvement of waterway conditions to enhance navigability and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DREDGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dredging is the process of removing sediment and debris from waterways to improve their navigability and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sediment is the material that needs to be removed from waterways to improve their navigability and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBRIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debris is another material that needs to be removed from waterways to improve their navigability and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDIMENT AND DEBRIS REMOVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sediment and Debris Removal is the combined process of removing both sediment and debris from waterways to improve their navigability and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED NAVIGATION AIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced Navigation Aids are sophisticated tools and systems used to improve the safety and efficiency of maritime navigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advanced Navigation Aids were installed as part of the Channel Mobility Improvement Program, enhancing navigation capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE CHANNEL MOBILITY IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Comprehensive Channel Mobility Improvement Program is a detailed plan to optimize waterway conditions for various maritime operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION OF USS NIMITZ (CVN-68)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Construction of USS Nimitz (CVN-68) is a significant event that required extensive channel mobility improvements to the waterway."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2003&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2003 marks the year when a comprehensive channel mobility improvement program was facilitated, indicating a significant event in maritime infrastructure development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL ASSOCIATION OF DREDGING COMPANIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The International Association of Dredging Companies published Advances in Dredging Technology in 1955, showcasing their contribution to dredging technology advancements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARITIME RESEARCH INSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Maritime Research Institute published The Impact of Channel Mobility Improvement on Ship Launching in 2010, emphasizing their research focus on channel improvements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASHINGTON, D.C.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Washington, D.C. is mentioned as the location where the Government Printing Office is based, indicating its significance in publishing government documents."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE HAGUE, NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Hague, Netherlands is mentioned as the location where the International Association of Dredging Companies is based, highlighting its international presence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROTTERDAM, NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rotterdam, Netherlands is the location where the Maritime Research Institute is based, underscoring its role in maritime research."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAVIGATION CHANNEL IMPROVEMENT STUDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Navigation Channel Improvement Study conducted by the United States Army Corps of Engineers in 1923 is a significant event in channel improvement projects."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCES IN DREDGING TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The publication of Advances in Dredging Technology by the International Association of Dredging Companies in 1955 is a significant event in the advancement of dredging technology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE IMPACT OF CHANNEL MOBILITY IMPROVEMENT ON SHIP LAUNCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The publication of The Impact of Channel Mobility Improvement on Ship Launching by the Maritime Research Institute in 2010 is a significant event in understanding channel improvements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Government Printing Office is based in Washington, D.C., and is responsible for publishing government documents."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANNEL MOBILITY IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Channel Mobility Improvement Program facilitated in 2003 is a significant event in maritime infrastructure development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0481</data>
    </node>
